WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.736
-My next guest stars in
the incredibly popular

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.136
television series "WandaVision."

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:07.840
The ninth and final episode of
Season 1 will be available

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.376
this Friday on Disney+.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:11.978
Here is Elizabeth Olsen!

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.113
Ah! That's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.915
Welcome, Elizabeth Olsen.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.083
Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:19.919
I'm happy to see you.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.353
Thank you so much, by the way,

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:24.023
for making the time to do
the "FallonVision" bit,

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.760
because it was awesome.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.994
-That was so fun.
-It's so much fun for us.

00:00:28.994 --> 00:00:31.464
But you -- I mean,
you went above and beyond

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.765
what we thought you would do.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:35.268
And, actually, we were
sending you wigs and stuff,

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.603
and because of COVID
and where you are,

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:38.804
it couldn't get there in time.

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:41.207
So you went straight to
the top and had some

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.743
"WandaVision" people
help you with it, right?

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.645
-Yeah, 'cause I'm filming
"Doctor Strange"

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.647
right now with
the women who were

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:52.318
the head of hair and makeup
departments on "WandaVision."

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:56.622
And, so, we were doing
six-day weeks here in London

00:00:56.622 --> 00:01:01.094
and we took our Sunday
to film it.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.830
And I didn't have
anything for the '70s,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.765
'cause there are no --
This is closed down.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.867
Everything's closed down.
Shops are closed down.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.069
You can't even
go to a thrift shop.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.905
And I had a bad idea
for the '70s,

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:15.441
and they thought I looked
not good enough.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.211
But they looked at
my dish towel in my kitchen

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.846
and they were like,
"That's your tube top.

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:24.249
You got to wear that
for the '70s."

00:01:24.249 --> 00:01:25.418 line:0%
I'm wearing a dishrag.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.719 line:0%
-I mean,
I did the scene with you,

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.522 line:0%
but I didn't realize that was
not a dress or tube top.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.056
That was a dishrag?
A dish towel?

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:32.158
-Yeah, it's a dishrag.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.827
And it just got underneath
my armpits.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:39.399
Like, in the back --
-We were this close.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:43.936
-Like, it doesn't even remotely
come together in the back.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.506
-So you're like this, like...

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:47.507
-I was.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.609
And I was so scared
to lift my arms,

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.645
that the whole thing
would come down.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.215
-Oh, my gosh! You got me!
See?

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.649
That's what you have to do
in these times.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.484
You got to be nimble.
You got to be quick.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:01.053
-Yeah.
-Oh, thank you.

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:02.555
Thank you again for doing that.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.990
It was a real treat
for all of us here.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.359
And, also, Kathryn Hahn
was awesome, as well,

00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:08.360
for helping us out.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.529
I know you're in England.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.130
You're filming
the "Doctor Strange" sequel.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.933
Can we say anything that --
Does "WandaVision"

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:17.336
have a connection to
the "Doctor Strange" sequel?

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:20.172
-It is a complete tee-up
for my character.

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:21.574
-There you go.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.975
I want to talk about
"WandaVision,"

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.311
'cause this is the biggest show
on television right now.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.846
Congrats with all the success.

00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:31.050
Did you expect the show
to be such a big hit?

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.719
-No. I expect everything
I do to fail.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.052
-Aha!

00:02:34.052 --> 00:02:39.158
-And I just try and hold on to
what I like about my job.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.360
And I just assume no one
is going to

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.263
enjoy anything I'm a part of.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.864
But we were really
swinging for the fences

00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:49.134
and felt really proud of
what we were doing.

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:54.607
And we felt like
it was different and unique

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.909
and there was
a great energy to it.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.712
But it --
You never know how something

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.380
is going to be received.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.216
And we also didn't predict that
there was going to be

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:06.118
a pandemic, where everyone is
going to be living in a bubble,

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:09.422
like our characters.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:13.259
And so it just kind of --
I feel like it was --

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.727
It came out at the right time.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.596
And it really was
a labor of love,

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.031
so I'm really proud of it.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.700
-I loved it.
I thought it was so good.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:25.104
There's only one episode left.
Episode 9 comes out this Friday.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.972
I'm assuming there's going to be

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:31.144
some closure to something or...

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.245
-I think so.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:36.782
I think there is --
I think it answers

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:39.818
the rest of the questions
that people might have

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:43.589
and leaves things open
the way Marvel needs to

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:47.125
to link everything back
into the films.

00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:49.361
And it's a Marvel finale.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.731
-After every episode
of "WandaVision,"

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.599
fans head straight to Twitter.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.768
I just thought I'd
run through a few tweets

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.738
and just see what your reaction
to some of them,

00:03:58.738 --> 00:03:59.772
just in case
you didn't see them.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.742
-Okay. I don't.
-This first one...

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.947
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.583
[ Cries ]

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.386
That is --
-That's like my first still.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.789
I think that's my
first movie still, like, ever.

00:04:17.789 --> 00:04:20.760
Like, was at Sundance.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.294
-That's good. It's you.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:26.031
It's acting. It's great.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:29.135
Oh, alright. This one I like.
It says...

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.805
It's like, Wait.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:33.873
How are you doing all these

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.474
bending around
and bending backwards,

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:40.879
and, at 18, this person's back
is already killing them?

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:43.916
-I mean, I don't remember
bending like that.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:47.887
That isn't anatomically
correct to my body.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.856
-No. That's something
that you've done --

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.323
Since the first time we saw you,

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:52.591
you've been doing these things.

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:54.627
And I go -- Yeah.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.528
Yeah, I mean,
you might be on wires,

00:04:56.528 --> 00:04:57.730
but you did it.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.367
It's like --
-It's crazy-looking.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.336
-Here's one that says...

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:07.606
It's like, "Wait.
Let me process.

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:11.143
Like, Huh? Wha-wha-what?"

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:13.979
-My mom just told me
the other day

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:18.417
that she's been calling me
the Red Witch for the last --

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.652
she said four years, but I think
I've been doing this

00:05:20.652 --> 00:05:22.254
for like six or seven.

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:23.956
And she just learned that

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:26.525
I was called
the Scarlet Witch last week.

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:29.395
-She's like,
"She plays Red Witch."

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.729
-Yeah.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:32.498
And she was like, "Why didn't
you ever correct me?"

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.401
And I just told her, "Because I
didn't know you were --

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.902
I just thought
you were making a joke."

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:38.003
I was like, "I didn't know

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:39.338
that's what you thought
my name was."

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:42.875
-"I love you too much, Mom."
And that's what moms do.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.877
I'm not going to correct you
at every single thing.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.078
Sure.

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:49.582
My dad still thinks
I'm Jimmy Kimmel.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.383
-Right.

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:53.719
-I'm not going to -- Why am I
going to correct him now?

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:58.357
He loves him.
Alright, let's see.

00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.792
Oh, this one made me laugh,

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:02.161
'cause I think it will
make you laugh, too.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.464
It says, "Marvel writers --
'So, how much pain should

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:06.632
we put Wanda through on her
journey to become

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.733
the Scarlet Witch?'

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.669
Marvel -- 'Yes.'"

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:12.271
It's just not even an answer.

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.540
It's like, "Yes, more pain."

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.743
-Ultimate, ultimate sad girl.

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:20.546
-And this one, I just think --
Everyone liked this one.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.514
It said, "Breaking news --
Elizabeth Olsen

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:24.817
is currently being
hospitalized due to carrying

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:26.952
the entire MCU on her back."

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:28.754
Yeah, that's your fans.

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.690
But that's the move!
That's the moves you're doing --

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.890
-That is the move.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.593
I guess I do that a lot,
don't I?

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:36.161
-Yeah. You do it,
but everyone loves you.

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:38.598
And It's great.
Including us.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:41.400
Congrats on all the success
with "WandaVision."

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.535
I want to show a clip.

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.603
Here is Elizabeth Olsen
in "WandaVision."

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:45.637
Take a look at this.

00:06:45.637 --> 00:06:47.273
-Is she asleep?

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:48.941
-Mommy's not sleeping, honey.

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:52.078
She's just resting her eyes.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:53.078
-Mom?

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:55.047
My head feels weird.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.149
It's, like, really noisy.

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:58.884
I don't like it.

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:03.322
-Resting her eyes.

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:05.791
As punishment
for my reckless evening,

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:09.529
I plan on taking a
quarantine-style staycation,

00:07:09.529 --> 00:07:14.967
a whole day just to myself.

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:16.469
That'll show me.

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:18.604
[ Sighs ]

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.640
♪♪

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.946
Oh, my God.

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.547
-Elizabeth Olsen, everybody.

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:31.117
Check out the season finale
of "WandaVision"

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:33.553
this Friday on Disney+.

